  deep:[{t:"p",text:"**uselist=False** makes the one-side attribute a single object (or None) instead of a list. It does not add uniqueness in the database; that comes from `unique=True` on the key. The default repr in Flask-SQLAlchemy 3 is `<Profile 1>`."}],
  remember:["Column ← id; relationship ← object.","backref creates the other attribute; back_populates needs both sides.","New objects have id None until written.","uselist=False → one object, not a list."],
  teachBack:{prompt:"Why does `Video(name=\"x\", channel=ch1)` fail while `Video(name=\"x\", playlist=ch1)` works?",model:"channel is an integer column, and SQLite cannot store a Channel object; playlist is the relationship, which takes the object and fills the key column with its id."},
